# T0 (the speed check of the production ENGINE): the production profile on the production base image, TIMED (no extent audit): warm-up, coding, the eight-live steady round, the audited-equal code round at 32k and 128k and the skewed round. Records the production-bytes round times and
# the concurrent8_code_equal hashes, the reference for any later window image. READ: every test completes, rounds with live=8 seen, no garbage or errored stream. Measured real time 25-31 min.
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the BASELINE EXTENSION window (README.md and ORDER.txt hold the window; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/baseline-ext and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN (ORDER.txt has each job's tag). Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards
# are resolved at run time. The extension runs ONLY on today's production ENGINE: every job serves the production base image tp4-serve-10 (the engine bytes are production's; production's thin layer on top of it is NOT exercised
# except in SR10, which replays it) and the production profile family c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix (the -audit twin where a gate needs the extent audit: the same engine and env plus audit flags). No window image is built. No job here moves :latest or places a model.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,concurrent8_steady,concurrent8_code_equal,concurrent8_code_32k,concurrent8_code_128k,concurrent8_skew
